presage flower","node":{"countryOfOrigin":"JP","description":null,"episodes":1,"format":"MOVIE","id":20791,"idMal":25537,"isAdult":false,"poster":"https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/media/anime/cover/medium/bx20791-yPCX5GJuMH2k.png","title":{"english":"Fate/stay night [Heaven's Feel] I. presage flower","native":"Fate/stay night[Heaven's Feel] Ⅰ.presage flower","romaji":"Fate/stay night [Heaven's Feel] I. presage flower","userPreferred":"Fate/stay night [Heaven's Feel] I. presage flower"}},"relationType":"ALTERNATIVE","resolved":true}],"schemaVersion":"1.1.0","score":{"scale":100,"source":"anilist","value":61},"season":"WINTER","seasonYear":2018,"series":["al-21717"],"seriesIds":[21717],"startDate":{"day":28,"month":1,"year":2018},"status":"FINISHED","studios":[{"animation":true,"id":44,"name":"Shaft"},{"animation":false,"id":17,"name":"Aniplex"},{"animation":false,"id":703,"name":"Notes"}],"synopsis":{"language":null,"source":"anilist","spoiler":false,"text":"A technological hell masquerading as paradise, Tsukimihara Academy is an artificial high school that serves as the setting for the next Holy Grail War. Created by the Moon Cell computer, the school is inhabited by Earth-projected souls who have even the slightest aptitude for being a \"Master.\" Of these 256 souls, 128 will be chosen for the main tournament and granted a Servant. With all of the Masters selected, the Academy activates a purge, targeting the remaining lifeforms for elimination.\n\nAwakening in a pool of his own blood, Hakuno Kishinami refuses to die. Fueled by unknown feelings of hatred, he vows to fight for survival. As he struggles to escape from a relentless pursuer, he finds a crimson blade plunged into the ground; and by pulling it out, Hakuno summons his own Servant, Saber, who instantly destroys his pursuer in a flurry of rose petals. With his newfound power, Hakuno must now begin his journey to Moon Cell's core, the Angelica Cage. There, he will unveil the reason for this artificial world and the secrets of his own blood-soaked past.\n\n(Source: MAL Rewrite)\n\nNotes:\n\n- Based on the video game Fate/Extra from 2010, however is not a direct adaptation, but one that diverges near the end of the game's narrative and follows a different continuity within the Fate/Extra setting.\n\n- Includes episodes 11-13, Illustrias Geocentric Theory.\n\n- The last episode aired with a runtime of 48 minutes as opposed to the standard 24."},"tags":[{"name":"Artificial Intelligence","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Body Horror","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Spearplay","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Dissociative Identities","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":75,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Post-Apocalyptic","rank":75,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Survival","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Virtual World","rank":68,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Dystopian","rank":66,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":66,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Nudity","rank":62,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Magic","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Amnesia","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Henshin","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Cosmic Horror","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Gore","rank":55,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Alternate Universe","rank":47,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Swordplay","rank":46,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Fate/EXTRA Last Encore","english":"Fate/EXTRA Last Encore","native":"Fate/EXTRA Last Encore","romaji":"Fate/EXTRA Last Encore","synonyms":[{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"Fate/EXTRA：最后安歌"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"命运/新章 最终回响"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"f/ele"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"fele"}]},"trailer":{"id":"PdXv5a5YMi4","site":"youtube","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/PdXv5a5YMi4/hqdefault.jpg"},"visibility":"general"}